Problem 1 — Employee Performance Analyzer
A company has recorded the performance scores of n employees for a month.

You are given an integer array scores.

Write a program that:

Finds the highest score.
Finds the lowest score.
Calculates the average score.
Counts how many employees scored above the average.
Searches for a given score and prints all indexes where it occurs.
Prints the scores in reverse order.

Example
Input:
scores = [70, 85, 90, 65, 90, 75]
target = 90

Output:
Highest Score = 90
Lowest Score = 65
Average = 79.16
Above Average = 3
Target found at indexes = [2, 4]
Reverse = [75, 90, 65, 90, 85, 70]
********************************************

Problem 2 — Monthly Sales Matrix
A company has 3 sales teams working for 4 weeks.
The sales data is:
int[][] sales = {
    {120, 150, 130, 170},
    {200, 180, 210, 190},
    {100, 140, 160, 120}
};

Where:
row    → employee/team
column → week


Write a program that:

Prints the complete matrix.
Finds the total sales of each team.
Finds the total sales of each week.
Finds the team with the highest total sales.
Finds the week with the highest total sales.
Finds the highest individual sale.
Prints the main diagonal only if the matrix is square.

Expected conceptual output
Team 1 Total = 570
Team 2 Total = 780
Team 3 Total = 520

Highest Team = Team 2

Week 1 Total = 420
Week 2 Total = 470
...
***********************************************

Problem 3 — Employee ID & Report Generator
You have employee records:

String[] names = {
    "Rahul",
    "Amit",
    "Priya",
    "Neha"
};

int[][] monthlyScores = {
    {80, 85, 90},
    {70, 75, 80},
    {95, 90, 92},
    {60, 65, 70}
};

Each row of monthlyScores belongs to the corresponding employee.

For example:
Rahul → 80, 85, 90
Amit  → 70, 75, 80
Priya → 95, 90, 92
Neha  → 60, 65, 70

Your task is to generate a complete employee report.

Expected output
===== EMPLOYEE PERFORMANCE REPORT =====

Employee: Rahul
Scores: 80, 85, 90
Total: 255
Average: 85.00
Status: EXCELLENT

Employee: Amit
Scores: 70, 75, 80
Total: 225
Average: 75.00
Status: GOOD

Employee: Priya
Scores: 95, 90, 92
Total: 277
Average: 92.33
Status: EXCELLENT

Employee: Neha
Scores: 60, 65, 70
Total: 195
Average: 65.00
Status: NEEDS IMPROVEMENT

Condition::::::::::
Status rules
Average >= 90 → EXCELLENT
Average >= 75 → GOOD
Average >= 60 → AVERAGE
Below 60     → NEEDS IMPROVEMENT












